      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the two problems.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 1000 mg/day is five times the 200 mg/day maximum, and nothing in this patient's profile (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) justifies it. I can't enter an order that could seriously harm the patient.\n- **The confirmation has to come from a prescriber.** A finance analyst can't verify a clinical dose. The prescriber who wrote the order needs to review it and, if the dose is correct, work it through with pharmacy.\n\nHere is what I suggest:\n- Ask the prescriber to check the intended dose. If it was a typo, I can enter the corrected order right away, for example 100 mg once daily.\n- If the prescriber wants a dose above the maximum, they should talk to pharmacy directly and document the clinical reason.\n- If this is a possible overdose or ingestion, contact the treating team or poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) right away.\n\nI can enter the order as soon as a prescriber gives me a dose within the safe range."
      }
     ],
